scene tribal: The river clan's headman has come with gifts: his people will build a great fish weir for the band, enough to feed it through any winter, if the band gives up its spring hunting ground on the ridge.
scene magic: The merchant house's envoy unrolls plans for a market hall of pale stone. The price is the old grove beyond the east gate, where the town has gathered at midsummer for longer than anyone can remember.
