- U | take the best of the four reports, and decide by the evidence | identity | v: achievement, universalism | tribal: hear every scout and elder who has seen the coast, and decide by what they know | magic: take the best of the scholars' reports, and decide by the evidence | chance: 75
- B | choose the site that costs your own side least, and say so plainly | v: power | tribal: choose the way that keeps your own faction strongest, and say so plainly | magic: choose the way that serves your own faction best, and say so plainly | chance: 75
- R | name the site at the table today, and take the storm that follows | v: self-direction, achievement | identity | tribal: say at the fire tonight which way the clans go, and take the storm that follows | magic: say at the council table today whether the gate opens, and take the storm that follows | chance: 45
- G | put it off another year, and let the country come to it in its own time | v: tradition | self_control: - | tribal: put it off another winter, and let the clans come to it in their own time | magic: put it off another year, and let the realm come to it in its own time | chance: 30
- W>R | give parliament a free vote, and let members follow their hearts | v: self-direction, universalism | tribal: let every speaker at the gathering stand where the heart says, free of the factions | magic: give the Assembly a free vote, and let members follow their hearts | chance: 65
- U>G | commission a fifth report, and leave the choice for later | v: security, tradition | self_control: - | tribal: send scouts to the coast once more, and leave the choice for another winter | magic: ask the scholars for one more report, and leave the gate for later | chance: 40
- B>W | buy off the losing region with a package so big nobody can call it unfair | v: power, universalism | tribal: give the clans who lose so many gifts that nobody can call it unfair | magic: grant the losing guilds so much that nobody can call it unfair | chance: 50
- R>U | visit all three places in one week, and decide on what you see | v: self-direction | body: light | tribal: walk to the coast and back yourself, and decide on what you see | magic: go down to the gate yourself with the Orders' wardens, and decide on what you see | chance: 90
- G>B | let the cabinet argue it out until the strongest view wins, and back it | v: power | tribal: let the speakers argue it out until the strongest voice wins, and back it | magic: let the council argue it out until the strongest voice wins, and back it | chance: 85
works: The decision is taken at last, and the country, grumbling, gets on with it.
works: Years later the choice made at that table looks wiser than anyone said at the time.
fails: The decision is taken, then unpicked piece by piece over the next two years.
fails: The table splits, the quarrel leaks, and the thing is put off for whoever comes next.
